---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

import ScreenGallery from "../../components/ScreenGallery.astro";
import LiveDemo from "../../components/LiveDemo.astro";
import CaseHero from "../../components/CaseHero.astro";
import FilmPlayer from "../../components/FilmPlayer.astro";
import SectionLabel from "../../components/SectionLabel.astro";

const IMG = "/images/work/design-ops";
// BASE_URL is "/" at root but "/repo" (no trailing slash) when ASTRO_BASE is set,
// so normalise it before concatenating or the path silently fuses: "/repodemo/".
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "") + "/";
---

<Base
  title="DRAFT — Turning live Jira boards into clear delivery decisions. Kishore Sudhamalla"
  description="A deterministic rule engine on a live Jira board, shipped and used weekly, with an AI layer on top that explains why a commitment moved, cites the records it read, writes back only after approval, and measures whether the fix held."
>

<style>
  .cs-label {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }
  .cs-h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .cs-lede { font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); }

  .draft-banner {
    background: #fdf8ea; border-bottom: 1px solid #e8d6a8; color: #8a6410;
    font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
  }
  :global(.dark) .draft-banner { background: rgba(220,180,80,.12); border-color: rgba(220,180,80,.3); color: #dcc07a; }

  .shot {
    margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden; background: var(--color-surface);
  }
  .shot img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .shot figcaption {
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-ink-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .shot-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .shot-grid--2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  /* numbered principle / bug rows */
  .rows { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .row {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem 2rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .row { grid-template-columns: 15rem 1fr; } }
  .row-t {
    font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .row-d { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); }

  .cards { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .cards--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } .cards--2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: 1.6rem; background: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .card-k {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3); margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .card-t {
    font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .card-b { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-2); }

  .stat-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr); gap: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden;
  }
  @media (min-width: 700px) { .stat-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .stat { background: var(--color-bg); padding: 1.6rem 1.4rem; }
  .stat-n {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .stat-l { font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .stat-s { font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-ink-3); }

  /* video */
  .demo { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 1.25rem; overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-surface); box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -40px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }
  :global(.dark) .demo { box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -35px rgba(0,0,0,.8); }
  .demo video { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  .quote {
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--color-ink);
    padding-left: 1.25rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* the eight rule flags */
  .flags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .flag {
    font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  /* rule-says / needed-to-know contrast. Plain text either side of a single
     divider, not two boxes: a card affordance on static prose read as
     clickable, which it isn't. */
  .split { display: grid; gap: 2rem 3rem; padding-top: 1.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .split-col { padding-left: 1.1rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border); }
  .split-col--alt { border-left-color: var(--color-ink); }
  .split-k {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3); margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .split-t {
    font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .split-b { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); }

  /* AI layers */
  .layers { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .layers { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .layers--3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .layers--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .layer {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 1.75rem; background: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .layer-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .layer-n {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }
  .layer-t {
    font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-ink); flex: 1;
  }
  .layer-s {
    font-size: 0.625rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase; border-radius: 100px; padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .layer-s--designed { color: #2f6b4a; background: #eef7f2; }
  .layer-s--next     { color: #6b6b64; background: var(--color-surface); }
  :global(.dark) .layer-s--designed { color: #8ecfab; background: rgba(90,170,124,.14); }
  :global(.dark) .layer-s--next     { color: #95958f; background: rgba(255,255,255,.06); }

  .layer-io { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .layer-io > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .layer-io dt {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3); padding-top: 0.1rem;
  }
  .layer-io dd {
    margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  /* small coloured icon chip, reused inside layer/card heads for the
     UX & IA trade-offs — same system as SectionLabel's chip. */
  .mini-icon {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mc) 16%, transparent);
    color: var(--mc);
  }
  :global(.dark) .mini-icon {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mc) 26%, transparent);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mc) 85%, white);
  }
  .mini-icon svg { width: 1rem; height: 1rem; }

  /* ── landscape table ── */
  .land { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .land-row {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  @media (min-width: 880px) { .land-row { grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr 1fr; } }
  .land-n { font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .land-a { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-2); }
  .land-b { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-3); }
  .land-h { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .land-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 0.7rem; }
    .land-h {
      display: block; font-size: 0.625rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.09em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3);
    }
  }

  /* ── signal derivability ── */
  .sig {
    display: grid; gap: 1px; background: var(--color-border);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .sig-r {
    background: var(--color-bg); padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.35rem 1.25rem; align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 840px) { .sig-r { grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr 10rem; align-items: center; } }
  .sig-n { font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .sig-d { font-size: 0.8438rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-2); }
  .sig-v {
    font-size: 0.625rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem; border-radius: 100px; border: 1px solid;
    justify-self: start; text-align: center;
  }
  .v-now { color: #2f6b4a; border-color: #b9d9c7; background: #eef7f2; }
  .v-src { color: #8a6410; border-color: #e8d6a8; background: #fdf8ea; }
  .v-no  { color: #b4462f; border-color: #e7bdb2; background: #fdf1ee; }
  :global(.dark) .v-now { color: #8ecfab; border-color: rgba(90,170,124,.35); background: rgba(90,170,124,.12); }
  :global(.dark) .v-src { color: #dcc07a; border-color: rgba(220,180,80,.35); background: rgba(220,180,80,.12); }
  :global(.dark) .v-no  { color: #e79a86; border-color: rgba(226,120,100,.35); background: rgba(226,120,100,.12); }

  /* summary on-ramp */
  .tldr {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-ink);
    padding: 0.35rem 0 0.35rem 1.6rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .tldr-k {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }
  .tldr-b {
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .tldr-b em { font-style: italic; }


  /* ── the one-way pipeline: rules produce truth, AI only annotates ── */
  .pipe { margin: 0; }
  .pipe-flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .pipe-flow {
      grid-auto-flow: column;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
  .pipe-node {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem; background: var(--color-bg); min-width: 0;
  }
  .pipe-n-t {
    font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .pipe-n-s { font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-ink-3); }

  /* Arrow: a rule plus a head, drawn in CSS so it inherits the ink colour.
     Vertical on narrow, horizontal once the row lays out side by side. */
  .pipe-arrow {
    position: relative; display: block;
    justify-self: center; align-self: center;
    width: 1px; height: 1.4rem;
    background: var(--color-ink-3);
    margin: 0.1rem 0;
  }
  .pipe-arrow::after {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: 0;
    width: 6px; height: 6px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-ink-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ink-3);
    transform: translate(-50%, 1px) rotate(45deg);
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .pipe-arrow { width: 2rem; height: 1px; margin: 0 0.55rem; }
    .pipe-arrow::after {
      left: auto; right: 0; bottom: 50%;
      transform: translate(1px, 50%) rotate(-45deg);
    }
  }
  /* the step into the AI layer is the one that changes character */
  .pipe-arrow--ai, .pipe-arrow--ai::after { border-color: var(--color-ink); }
  .pipe-arrow--ai { background: var(--color-ink); }

  .pipe-cap {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }
  .pipe-cap-x {
    flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink-3); line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .stack { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .stack span {
    font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 100px; padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;
  }

  /* ── the PRD this shipped against ── */
  .prd { counter-reset: prd; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.75rem; }
  .prd-item { counter-increment: prd; position: relative; padding-left: 2.75rem; }
  .prd-item::before {
    content: counter(prd); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.1rem;
    width: 2rem; height: 2rem; border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-ink-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono, inherit); font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  }
  .prd-head { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .prd-t {
    font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .prd-badge {
    font-size: 0.625rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 100px;
  }
  .prd-badge--new       { color: #3157c7; background: #eaeffc; }
  .prd-badge--timeless   { color: #2f6b4a; background: #eef7f2; }
  .prd-badge--upgraded   { color: #8a6410; background: #fdf8ea; }
  .prd-badge--merged     { color: #b4582f; background: #fdeee6; }
  :global(.dark) .prd-badge--new       { color: #a9bdf5; background: rgba(60,95,220,.16); }
  :global(.dark) .prd-badge--timeless  { color: #8ecfab; background: rgba(90,170,124,.14); }
  :global(.dark) .prd-badge--upgraded  { color: #dcc07a; background: rgba(220,180,80,.14); }
  :global(.dark) .prd-badge--merged    { color: #e79a6e; background: rgba(226,140,80,.14); }
  .prd-b { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .prd-b:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .prd-b b { color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 600; font-style: normal; }
  .prd-b em { font-style: italic; }
  .prd-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .prd-list li { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); }
  .prd-list li b { color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 600; }

  .prd-callout {
    margin-top: 0.5rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-ink);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }
  .prd-callout b { color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 700; }
</style>

<div class="draft-banner">Draft for review — not the live page. Compare against /work/design-ops.</div>

  <!-- Back -->
  <div class="container-pg pt-8">
    <a href="/#work" class="cs-label inline-flex items-center gap-2 hover:text-[var(--color-ink)] transition-colors">
      <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M8.5 2L3.5 7L8.5 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      Back to work
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
  <CaseHero
    eyebrow="Design ops · Systems · AI-native UX"
    title="Turning live Jira boards into clear delivery decisions."
    lede="I designed and built a system that reads a live Jira board. The Jira sync and deterministic rule engine are shipped and used weekly: that part is done and running. On that same live data, I then added the layer I actually wanted to design: an AI that explains why a commitment moved, cites the records it read, and proposes one action, a working prototype today with the model call stubbed. Nothing writes back without human-in-the-loop approval of the exact change, and the system measures whether the fix held."
    meta={[
      { k: "Role", v: "UX designer, solo, end to end" },
      { k: "Shipped", v: "Jira sync & rule engine, in daily use. AI layer is a live prototype" },
      { k: "Scope", v: "Jira sync → intelligence layer" },
      { k: "Users", v: "A working design org" },
    ]}
    img={`${IMG}/hero-window.webp`}
    alt="Design Ops, delivery overview"
    cards={[
      {
        eyebrow: "AI · root cause (prototype)",
        value: "High",
        label: "Requirements weren't ready",
        note: "Cited: two date changes, 27 days of slip, and the ticket's own note.",
      },
      {
        eyebrow: "Verified",
        value: "27d",
        label: "The intervention did not hold",
        note: "The loop measures its own advice, and reports when it failed.",
      },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="pb-4" data-reveal>
    <div class="container-pg">
      <!-- On-ramp: the payoff otherwise doesn't land until deep in the page. -->
      <div class="tldr">
        <p class="tldr-k">In short</p>
        <p class="tldr-b">
          The weekly delivery review used to start by rebuilding the picture by hand from
          a Jira export. It now starts from the decisions. The rule engine behind that is
          shipped. The AI explanation layer on top is a working prototype on the same live
          data, called out again where it matters below.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ WATCH ══ -->
  <section class="sec-y" data-reveal>
    <div class="container-pg">
      <p class="cs-label mb-3">Shipped, in daily use</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2 mb-4 max-w-2xl">See it first.</h2>
      <p class="cs-lede max-w-2xl mb-8">
        A two minute tour of every feature, from Jira setup to the decision log. Then the
        real tool, running on sample data.
      </p>

      <div class="demo mb-4" data-reveal>
        <FilmPlayer src={`${IMG}/ops-demo.mp4`} poster={`${IMG}/ops-demo-poster.jpg`} label="A two minute animated tour of every Design Ops feature with music: Jira setup, pods, quarter planning, delivery tracking, the work view, ticket drill-down, the executive summary, the eight rule flags, asking the board, root-cause explanations, an agent that proposes a change, the approval step, and the decision log that measures whether it worked" />
      </div>
      <p class="cs-label mb-12">Tour with sound. Press play.</p>

      <p class="cs-lede max-w-2xl mb-6">
        Now use it yourself. Switch the quarter, open a ticket that has slipped, regroup
        the board by designer, ask it a question.
      </p>

      <LiveDemo
        {/* index.html explicitly: the dev server does not resolve directory indexes
            under public/, and naming the file works on static hosts too. */}
        src={`${BASE}demo/design-ops/index.html`}
        title="Design Ops dashboard, live demo running on sample data"
        hint="The real tool, running on sample data. Change the quarter, open a ticket, use the board."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 01 PROBLEM ══ -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] sec-y" data-reveal>
    <div class="container-pg">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.3fr] gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24">
          <SectionLabel icon="context">01. The problem</SectionLabel>
          <h2 class="cs-h2 mb-6">Jira reports tickets.<br>It doesn't report a team.</h2>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-2)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Running design delivery meant rebuilding the same picture by hand every week.
            Export. Pivot. Chase. Jira's own dashboards are too generic or too heavy to
            set up and none of them speak design ops: no hi-fi commitments, no pods, no
            T-shirt sizing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-ink-2)] leading-relaxed">
            It cost more than time. Designers felt ambushed by Jira dates nobody had
            looked at since they were set, and the first half of the review went to
            arguing whose numbers were right instead of unblocking anyone's work.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rows">
          {[
            ["Are we actually on pace?", "Delivery rate against what was committed, with working days and time off counted."],
            ["Who is quietly overloaded?", "Capacity spread across a team, visible before someone burns out."],
            ["What has already slipped?", "Commitments that moved without anyone noticing."],
            ["What genuinely changed?", "Which fields moved on a ticket, when and by whom. The history behind a date."],
            ["Are the estimates real?", "T-shirt sizes checked against the working days the team has actually delivered."],
          ].map(([t, d]) => (
            <div class="row">
              <p class="row-t">{t}</p>
              <p class="row-d">{d}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 02 THE PRD ══ -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] sec-y" data-reveal>
    <div class="container-pg">
      <SectionLabel icon="craft">02. The PRD this shipped against</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="cs-h2 mb-4 max-w-2xl">Written before the prototype existed.</h2>
      <p class="cs-lede max-w-2xl mb-12">
        Solo and unassigned, so nobody was going to ask for this document. Wrote it anyway,
        in the 2026 shape: the prototype above shows <em>what</em>. This is the <em>why</em>,
        <em>how it's measured</em>, and <em>when it would get rolled back</em>.
      </p>

      <ol class="prd">
        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">The decision this records</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--new">New</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b">
            We built two versions: a rule-only risk engine, and a second layer that explains
            what the rules flagged instead of flagging anything itself. Shipping the second,
            because a wrong model output should be able to change the wording of a risk and
            never its existence.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Opportunity framing</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--timeless">Timeless</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Core problem:</b> Jira reports tickets, not whether a team is on pace.</p>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Data:</b> the weekly review was a rebuilt-by-hand export, every time. Three real
            moments exposed the gap: <em>"Jira says 74, this shows 84"</em> (a pagination bug
            double-counting tickets), an offhand comment about one overdue ticket that led to a
            "today" constant frozen since the build (every date calc quietly said on track,
            forever), and "status says at risk, detail shows nothing" surfacing from three views
            that each derived risk differently.
          </p>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Hypothesis:</b> if delivery status came from one system instead of a rebuilt export, slips would surface when they happened, not in the review where it's already too late to act.</p>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Strategy fit:</b> extends the system the team already lives in (Jira) rather than replacing it, which is the lowest-friction way to get an unsponsored internal tool actually adopted.</p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">The prototype</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--new">New</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Link:</b> the two-minute tour and the live demo above, running on sample data:
            Jira sync, the delivery view, a root-cause explanation, the approval step, and the
            decision log that checks its own advice.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Features &amp; behaviour contract</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--timeless">Timeless</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Edge cases found building it:</b> a hardcoded "today" that never advanced, the same
            risk bug rediscovered in three separate views before fixing all three at once, and a
            sync that could double-count a ticket edited mid-page.
          </p>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Tracking:</b> every changelog field move, every AI decision (accept, investigate,
            dismiss), the baseline captured at decision time, and the verified outcome against it.
          </p>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Behaviour contract:</b> for "Dates Drifted," input is a changelog with three date
            moves. Good output cites the PRD change and the concurrent-load note, at high
            confidence. Bad output asserts a cause with nothing cited. Reject condition: any
            output that writes to Jira without a human approving the exact record first.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Success measurement &amp; evals</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--upgraded">Upgraded</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Metric to graduate:</b> the signal a decision targeted moves favourably against the
            baseline captured at decision time, "Held," not just the absence of complaints.
            Guardrail: never return a verdict before enough time has passed to judge it. V1
            declared "Held" the moment a decision was made, since nothing had moved yet; it now
            says "too early to judge" and waits.
          </p>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Golden set:</b> all three decision types run against sample tickets with every
            citation checked by hand before trusting the output shape. The model call itself is
            currently stubbed, so this evaluates the interaction design, not a model's accuracy,
            flagged as a known gap rather than hidden.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Scope &amp; non-goals</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--merged">Merged</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>In:</b> Jira sync, the rule engine, delivery and capacity views, root-cause explanation, the weekly paragraph, ask-the-board, and the decision log with approval-gated write-back.</p>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Non-goals, cut on purpose because the data behind them doesn't exist yet:</b></p>
          <ul class="prd-list">
            <li><b>Design-system deviation</b>, needs component-adoption data from Figma, a second integration.</li>
            <li><b>Alignment risk</b>, needs initiatives linked to product priorities, a link that rarely exists without deliberate tagging.</li>
            <li><b>Strategic vs. reactive mix and design debt</b>, no agreed definition or consistent tagging exists; any number here would be invented.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Side effect worth accepting:</b> state lives in memory, snapshotted to localStorage, single-machine by design, a real tradeoff for zero infrastructure cost on a tool nobody else is paid to maintain.</p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Rollout &amp; rollback</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--timeless">Timeless</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Exposure:</b> one working design org, Jira sync live, used weekly in the delivery review.</p>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Ramp gate:</b> earns continued use by removing the manual rebuild, not by clearing a target number set in advance.</p>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Kill switch:</b> unnecessary by design. The ticket panel is read-only with one "Open in Jira" link, and nothing writes until a person approves the exact record, so there's no autonomous action to roll back.</p>
        </li>

        <li class="prd-item">
          <div class="prd-head">
            <p class="prd-t">Release criteria &amp; change log</p>
            <span class="prd-badge prd-badge--timeless">Timeless</span>
          </div>
          <p class="prd-b"><b>Definition of done:</b> the Jira sync, rule engine and views ship and hold up in daily use, confirmed by using it in a real weekly review rather than a demo of one.</p>
          <p class="prd-b">
            <b>Change log:</b> v1, the rule engine, shipped and in daily use. v2, this AI
            explanation, decision, approval and verification loop, is a working prototype on the
            same live data with the model call stubbed. Not built yet: a real model call,
            semantic field mapping, per-person cadence anomalies, probabilistic landing.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="prd-callout mt-12">
        <b>The rule I held this to:</b> every claim above has to trace to something earlier on
        this page, a quote, a bug, a screen, a cut feature. If I couldn't point to where a line
        came from, it didn't go in. The gap people used to fill with "trust me" is the one this
        page is written to close.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ══ 03 LANDSCAPE ══ -->
  <section class="sec-y" data-reveal>
    <div class="container-pg">
      <SectionLabel icon="systems">03. What already exists</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="cs-h2 mb-4 max-w-3xl">I checked before building anything.</h2>
      <p class="cs-lede max-w-2xl mb-12">
        It mostly exists in pieces. None of the pieces treats the design workflow itself as
        the unit of analysis. Design Intelligence is not my idea. The DesignOps field has
        argued for it for years. The need is documented and the product is not, and that
        gap is the only thing I set out to claim.
      </p>

      <div class="land-head">
        <span class="land-h">Category</span>
        <span class="land-h">What it optimises for</span>
        <span class="land-h">What it leaves open</span>
      </div>
      <div class="land">
        {[
          ["Jira dashboards &amp; Advanced Roadmaps",
           "Ticket state, sprint burn-down, plan against actual across a portfolio.",
           "Treats a design ticket like any ticket. No design stages, rework or skipped validation."],
          ["Resource tools: Float, Runn, Mosaic, Asana, Adobe Workfront",
           "Allocation and utilisation: who is booked, for how long, on which project.",
           "Capacity as hours, not as context-switching or the balance of strategic against reactive work."],
          ["Figma ↔ Jira integration",
           "Connecting design files to delivery tickets so context travels with the work.",
           "Linkage, not interpretation. Says nothing about flow or health."],
          ["Design-system analytics",
           "Component adoption and detachment.",
           "Scoped to the file. Silent on whether the workflow producing the files is working."],
