          <div class="pipe-node">
            <p class="pipe-n-t">AI layer</p>
            <p class="pipe-n-s">What it means, and why</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="pipe-cap">
          <span class="pipe-cap-x" aria-hidden="true">✕</span>
          <span>
            No arrow points back. AI reads the flags and never sets one. A wrong model
            output can change the wording of a risk and never its existence.
          </span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="split mt-12">
        <div class="split-col">
          <p class="split-k">Stays rule-based, permanently</p>
          <p class="split-t">Anything you'd defend in a review</p>
          <p class="split-b">
            Whether a date has passed. Whether scope changed. Capacity and working-day
            maths. Whether something was delivered. A human can trace exactly how.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-col split-col--alt">
          <p class="split-k">Becomes AI</p>
          <p class="split-t">Anything requiring judgement or language</p>
          <p class="split-b">
            Why something slipped. What to say about it. What is unusual for a particular
            person. Every output cites the ticket, comment or date change it read, because
            an explanation you can't verify is worse than none.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="cs-label mt-16 mb-3">Three things it does</p>
